
.meta{
  title: "ChRIS: An Overview for HARBOR"
  theme: "command-line"
  transition: zoom
  label: "rudolph@artemis: ~ {n} {spoke}"
  typography:
    baseline: presentation
  snippets:
    marker: "▸ "
  css:
    "#slide-1 h1":
        font-size: "2.6em"
    ".slide .term pre.fig":
        color: "#d4d4d4"
        line-height: "1.25"
        overflow: "visible"
        margin: "0.2em 0 0.8em 1.6em"
    ".slide .term pre.fig b":
        color: "#4ec9b0"
        font-weight: "400"
    ".slide .term pre.fig u":
        display: "inline-block"
        width: "1ch"
        text-decoration: "none"
        color: "#4ec9b0"
    ".slide .term pre.fig i":
        color: "#858585"
        font-style: "normal"
    ".slide .term pre.fig.wide":
        font-size: "0.72em"
        line-height: "1.2"
        margin-left: "0"
}

.slide{
  .label{rudolph@artemis: ~/harbor}
  .title{Boot}
  .body{
    .h1{ChRIS}
    .h2{An overview for the HARBOR consortium}

    .div{.class{dim} Rudolph Pienaar -- Boston Children's Hospital / Harvard Medical School}

    .term{
.typewriter{$> ./chris --overview --audience=harbor}
    }
  }
}

.slide{
  .title{TL;DR}
  .body{
    .h1{The Short Version}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --tldr}
      .o{Analyses run .bf{next to the data}.}
      .o{One .bf{rule}: read a directory, write one, exit.}
      .o{Chain them. The tree .bf{is} the provenance.}
      .o{In HARBOR: the runtime inside .bf{every} Trusted Domain.}
    }

    .takeaway{OPENSHIFT GOVERNS THE CLUSTER. ChRIS MAKES THE SCIENCE ON IT AUDITABLE.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{outline}
  .title{Outline}
  .body{
    .h1{Outline}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --outline}
    .nexus{.id{outline}
      .div{.jump{.target{lightness} The Unbearable Lightness of Defining}}
      .div{.jump{.target{what-is} What Is ChRIS?}}
      .div{.jump{.target{contract} The App Contract}}
      .div{.jump{.target{workflows} Workflows and Provenance}}
      .div{.jump{.target{architecture} Architecture}}
      .div{.jump{.target{mise} mise: ChRIS as a Computer}}
      .div{.jump{.target{clinic} ChRIS in the Clinic}}
      .div{.jump{.target{harbor} Where ChRIS Sits in HARBOR}}
      .div{.jump{.target{roadmap} What HARBOR Adds to ChRIS}}
      .div{.jump{.target{working} Working With It}}
      .div{.jump{.target{conclusions} Conclusions}}
    }
    }
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{lightness}
  .title{The Unbearable Lightness of Defining}
  .body{
    .h1{The Unbearable Lightness of Defining}
    .h2{What is an iPad? Everyone knows. Now define it.}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> whatis ipad}
    .nexus{.id{ipad-answers}
      .div{.jump{.target{mobile-os} "It's a Mobile OS"}}
      .div{.jump{.target{pictures} "It's Pictures You Touch"}}
      .div{.jump{.target{crippled-mac} "It's a Crippled Mac"}}
      .div{.jump{.target{so-chris} So What Is ChRIS?}}
    }
    }
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mobile-os}
  .title{It's a Mobile OS}
  .body{
    .h1{"It's a Mobile OS"}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> define "mobile OS"}
      .o{Fine. What is a .bf{mobile} OS?}
      .o{Different in kind? Or a smaller .bf{case}?}
      .o{A laptop is mobile. macOS .bf{isn't} one.}
      .o{One undefined word .bf{traded} for another.}
    }
    .takeaway{NAMING THE CATEGORY ISN'T DEFINING THE THING.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{pictures}
  .title{It's Pictures You Touch}
  .body{
    .h1{"It's Pictures You Touch"}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> describe --by=experience ipad}
      .o{A screen of little .bf{pictures}.}
      .o{Touch one. It .bf{does} a thing.}
      .o{So is any tablet. Any .bf{phone}.}
      .o{Honest. It describes what people .bf{met}.}
    }
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{pictures-2}
  .title{Now Change the UI}
  .body{
    .h1{Now Change the UI}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> launcher --replace}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 ┌──────────────────────┐            ┌──────────────────────┐
 │ [wx]   [news] [game] │            │ $ weather            │
 │ [mail] [maps] [cam]  │   ─────<u>▶</u>   │ $ news               │
 │ [web]  [pay]  [chat] │            │ $ _                  │
 └──────────────────────┘            └──────────────────────┘
  <i>pictures you touch</i>                  <i>a prompt you type at</i>
</pre>}
      .o{Mine runs .bf{Re:T-UI}: no icons, a prompt.}
      .o{Same hardware. Same .bf{apps}.}
      .o{No pictures. Still a .bf{phone}.}
    }
    .takeaway{PEOPLE DEFINE A THING BY HOW THEY MET IT.}
    .source{Re:T-UI launcher guide, re-tui.pages.dev}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{crippled-mac}
  .title{It's a Crippled Mac}
  .body{
    .h1{"It's a Crippled Mac"}
    .h2{The architect's answer}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> describe --by=construction ipad}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>macOS</b>     child processes  ·  pipes  ·  one filesystem  ·  any UI you like
   │       <i>same kernel (XNU), same core (Darwin)</i>
   <u>▼</u>
 <b>iPadOS</b>    every app sandboxed  ·  no child processes  ·  a private container each
</pre>}
      .o{A close .bf{relative} of macOS.}
      .o{No .bf{fork}. No pipes. No shared files.}
      .o{For security: a .bf{crippled} Mac.}
      .o{Subjective too. An .bf{architect's} view.}
    }
    .source{Apple Platform Security, "Security of runtime process in iOS, iPadOS, and visionOS" · apple-oss-distributions/xnu · Apple Developer Forums thread 747499}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{crippled-mac-2}
  .title{Which Definition Survives?}
  .body{
    .h1{Which Definition Survives?}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> diff --swap-ui experience construction}
      .o{Swap the launcher. "Pictures" is now .bf{false}.}
      .o{"No pipes, no shared files" is still .bf{true}.}
      .o{Experience describes the .bf{interface}.}
      .o{Construction says what it .bf{can} do.}
    }
    .takeaway{KEEP THE DEFINITION THAT SURVIVES A CHANGE OF UI.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{so-chris}
  .title{So What Is ChRIS?}
  .body{
    .h1{So What Is ChRIS?}
    .h2{Ask five people. Each names what they met.}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> whatis chris --ask=5}
      .o{"A dashboard for running analyses." .bf{ChRIS_ui}}
      .o{"A full web UI with a shell. It looks like a whole computer." .bf{ARGUS}}
      .o{"The thing that pulls studies out of a PACS from the CLI." .bf{chell}}
      .o{"A persistent record of all analyses and transformations." .bf{a feed}}
      .o{"A workflow engine." .bf{a pipeline}}
      .o{All true. All .bf{pictures} you touch.}
    }
    .takeaway{DEFINE ChRIS THE WAY AN ARCHITECT DEFINES AN iPad.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{so-chris-2}
  .title{The Same Move, Reversed}
  .body{
    .h1{The Same Move, Reversed}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> diff ipad chris --app-model}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>iPad</b>     [app]  │  [app]  │  [app]      <i>walls between apps: isolation</i>
 <b>ChRIS</b>    [app] ──<u>▶</u> [app] ──<u>▶</u> [app]      <i>a directory handed on: composition</i>
</pre>}
      .o{iPad: apps .bf{forbidden} to share.}
      .o{ChRIS: apps .bf{required} to hand on.}
      .o{Same strictness. Opposite .bf{direction}.}
      .o{ChRIS .bf{is} the pipe.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE APP MODEL IS THE DEFINITION. THE UI IS ONE WAY TO MEET IT.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{what-is}
  .title{What Is ChRIS?}
  .body{
    .h1{What Is ChRIS?}
    .h2{ChRIS Research Integration Service}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> whatis chris}
      .o{.bf{Open-source}. Computation where the data must stay.}
      .o{Boston Children's, .bf{Red Hat}, Mass Open Cloud.}
      .o{Programs with no .bf{interaction}: args in, files out.}
      .o{That is most of research imaging. And most of .bf{ingestion}.}
    }
    .source{FNNDSC/CHRIS_docs · Pienaar et al., IEEE EMBC 2015}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{what-is-2}
  .title{Where It Came From}
  .body{
    .h1{Where It Came From}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> git log --oneline --reverse chris}
      .o{.span{.class{dim} pre-2010} .bf{bash} scripts as glue.}
      .o{.span{.class{dim} 2010 v1} a web front end, one .bf{HPC}.}
      .o{.span{.class{dim} 2013 v2} .bf{feeds} and plugins arrive.}
      .o{.span{.class{dim} 2017 v3} REST and .bf{containers}. Any cluster.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE GLUE KEPT OUTGROWING THE TOOLS. SO THE GLUE BECAME THE PLATFORM.}
    .source{FNNDSC/CHRIS_docs, History · Pienaar et al., LNCS 10494, 2017 (CHIPS)}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{contract}
  .title{The App Contract}
  .body{
    .h1{The App Contract}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> app [--flags] /input /output}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
   /input              ┌───────────────────────┐              /output
 ┌─────────┐           │ <b>plugin</b>: one container │           ┌─────────┐
 │  files  │ ────────<u>▶</u> │ app --flags           │ ────────<u>▶</u> │  files  │
 └─────────┘           │ runs once, then exits │           └─────────┘
                       └───────────────────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{A .bf{container}: read a directory, write one, exit.}
      .o{It doesn't know ChRIS .bf{exists}.}
      .o{A JSON .bf{descriptor}: parameters, CPU, memory, GPU.}
      .o{Any .bf{language}. Same boundary.}
    }
    .takeaway{IF IT RUNS IN A CONTAINER AND WRITES FILES, IT CAN BE A PLUGIN.}
    .source{ChRIS Plugin Specification, FNNDSC/CHRIS_docs (specs/ChRIS_Plugins.adoc)}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{contract-2}
  .title{Three Kinds of Plugin}
  .body{
    .h1{Three Kinds of Plugin}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris plugin --types}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>fs</b>                     <b>ds</b>                          <b>ts</b>
 [app] ──<u>▶</u> /out         /in ──<u>▶</u> [app] ──<u>▶</u> /out      /in ─┐
                                                    /in ─┼<u>▶</u> [app] ──<u>▶</u> /out
                                                    /in ─┘
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{fs}: brings data in. No input directory.}
      .o{.bf{ds}: input in, output out. Nearly everything.}
      .o{.bf{ts}: reshapes the graph. Joins branches.}
      .o{De-id, conversion, segmentation: all .bf{ds}.}
    }
    .source{ChRIS Plugin Specification, "Plugin Type"}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{contract-end}
  .title{Wrap Before Inventing}
  .body{
    .h1{Wrap Before Inventing}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> cat plugin-doctrine.txt}
      .o{ChRIS needn't .bf{own} every tool.}
      .o{A good tool gets a .bf{container} and an interface.}
      .o{It gains recorded parameters and a pinned .bf{version}.}
      .o{Write new only when .bf{nothing} fits.}
    }
    .takeaway{NOT "DID WE WRITE IT?" BUT "DOES IT OBEY THE CONTRACT?"}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{workflows}
  .title{Workflows and Provenance}
  .body{
    .h1{Workflows and Provenance}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> tree feed/}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>feed</b>
 └─ pacs-pull              <i>fs   brings the study in</i>
    └─ dicom-normalise     <i>ds</i>
       └─ de-identify      <i>ds</i>
          ├─ segment       <i>ds</i>
          │  └─ measure    <i>ds</i>
          └─ embed         <i>ds   every node keeps its own output directory</i>
</pre>}
      .o{A .bf{tree} of runs. Output feeds input.}
      .o{In HARBOR's terms: apps talk through .bf{storage}.}
      .o{Every intermediate output stays .bf{inspectable}.}
      .o{A .bf{feed} is one run. A pipeline is its template.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE UNIX PIPE, STRETCHED ACROSS A CLUSTER.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{workflows-2}
  .title{Data State, Not Control Flow}
  .body{
    .h1{Data State, Not Control Flow}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> diff control-flow data-state}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>control flow</b>    [A] ──ok?──<u>▶</u> [B] ──ok?──<u>▶</u> [C]
                 <i>a controller decides what runs next</i>

 <b>data state</b>      /d0 ──A──<u>▶</u> /d1 ──B──<u>▶</u> /d2 ──C──<u>▶</u> /d3
                 <i>every arrow leaves a directory behind</i>
</pre>}
      .o{Control flow: Argo, Tekton. Data state: .bf{Make}, ChRIS.}
      .o{Done when the output is on .bf{disk}.}
      .o{Gates and joins are .bf{plugins}. So they're recorded.}
      .o{The cost: a .bf{step} where Argo needs a line.}
    }
    .takeaway{WHAT RAN, IN WHAT ORDER AND WHY: READ IT OFF THE DATA.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{workflows-end}
  .title{The Five Questions}
  .body{
    .h1{The Five Questions}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> provenance --explain result.dcm}
      .o{What data went .bf{in}?}
      .o{Which app, which .bf{version}?}
      .o{With what .bf{parameters}?}
      .o{What came .bf{out}?}
      .o{Answered by walking a .bf{directory} tree.}
    }
    .takeaway{MAKE THE HANDOFFS BORING. MAKE THE DATA STATE EXPLICIT.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{architecture}
  .title{Architecture}
  .body{
    .h1{Architecture}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --components}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 ┌──────────┐  REST  ┌──────────────────────────────┐  DICOM  ┌────────┐
 │ ChRIS_ui │ ─────<u>▶</u> │             <b>CUBE</b>             │ <u>◀</u>────── │  PACS  │
 │   mise   │        │ users files feeds provenance │  <i>pfdcm</i>  └────────┘
 └──────────┘        └───────┬──────────────┬───────┘ <i>oxidicom</i>
                             │              │
                         ┌───┴───┐      ┌───┴───┐
                         │ pfcon │      │ pfcon │   <i>one per</i>
                         └───┬───┘      └───┬───┘   <i>compute environment</i>
                         OpenShift         HPC
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{CUBE}: one REST API over everything.}
      .o{.bf{pfcon}: runs the job, Docker to SLURM.}
      .o{.bf{pfdcm, oxidicom}: the PACS bridge.}
    }
    .source{FNNDSC/CHRIS_docs · FNNDSC/pfcon · FNNDSC/oxidicom · HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{architecture-end}
  .title{Who Owns What}
  .body{
    .h1{Who Owns What}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --layers}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>CUBE</b>       meaning      which app, which directory, which parameters
   <u>▼</u>
 <b>pfcon</b>      mapping      that run, on this backend
   <u>▼</u>
 <b>cluster</b>    execution    pods, storage, policy
</pre>}
      .o{CUBE owns .bf{meaning}. pfcon maps it. The cluster runs it.}
      .o{One CUBE, several .bf{compute} environments.}
      .o{The lock-in test: does it run .bf{without} Kubernetes?}
    }
    .takeaway{REPLACE MECHANISMS FREELY. DON'T REPLACE THE MEANING OF THE WORKFLOW.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise}
  .title{mise: ChRIS as a Computer}
  .body{
    .h1{mise: ChRIS as a Computer}
    .h2{Drive ChRIS like a computer, not a web API}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> man mise}
    .nexus{.id{mise-parts}
      .div{.jump{.target{mise-machine} A Machine, Not an Endpoint}}
      .div{.jump{.target{mise-layers} Above CUBE}}
      .div{.jump{.target{mise-stack} The Whole Stack}}
      .div{.jump{.target{mise-kernel} The Intent Kernel}}
      .div{.jump{.target{mise-intent} One Intent, Four Ways}}
      .div{.jump{.target{mise-session} One Session, Many Surfaces}}
      .div{.jump{.target{mise-door} The Door and the Berth}}
    }
    }
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-machine}
  .title{A Machine, Not an Endpoint}
  .body{
    .h1{A Machine, Not an Endpoint}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chell}
      .o{.typewriter{chris@cube:...loads$ cd ~/uploads/SAG-anon}}
      .o{.typewriter{chris@cube:...-anon$ ls /bin | head -3
 adc-to-zmap-nii-scale-up-v0.1.0
 adc-to-zmap-nii-scale-up-v0.2.1
 adc-to-zmap-nii-scale-up-v0.2.2}}
      .o{.typewriter{chris@cube:...-anon$ whatif pl-fshack-v1.5.0 --inputFile brain.mgz
  on   a new feed, rooted by pl-dircopy of /home/chris/uploads/SAG-anon
whatif: pl-fshack-v1.5.0 was not run; nothing was created}}
      .o{.typewriter{chris@cube:...-anon$ cat /proc/jobs/feed_123/pl-dircopy_788/pl-fshack_789/status
finishedSuccessfully}}
    }
    .takeaway{DATA IS A FILESYSTEM. A PLUGIN IS A COMMAND. A JOB IS A FILE.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-layers}
  .title{Above CUBE}
  .body{
    .h1{Above CUBE}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> mise --layers}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>chell  argus</b>   how you look       a terminal, a browser
   <u>▲</u>
 <b>calypso</b>        who is there       one login, one live session
   <u>▲</u>
 <b>mise</b>           where things are   /home  /bin  /proc
   <u>▲</u>
 <b>CUBE</b>           what is true       the objects and the laws between them
</pre>}
      .o{Below CUBE, swap the .bf{cluster}.}
      .o{Above CUBE, swap the .bf{surface}.}
    }
    .takeaway{CUBE SAYS WHAT IS TRUE. mise SAYS WHERE THINGS ARE.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-stack}
  .title{The Whole Stack}
  .body{
    .h1{The Whole Stack}
    .h2{Three machines, two networks}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> mise --stack}
<pre class="fig wide">
 ┌─ <b>your machine</b> ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   <i>a terminal, a browser,</i>
 │ ┌──────────┐                           you                                       │   <i>and programs of your own</i>
 │ │ a program│                            │                                        │
 │ └─┬────────┘                   ┌────────┴────────┐                               │
 │   ┆ ┌──────────┐               │                 │                               │
 │   ┆ │ a program│         ┌─────┴─────┐     ┌─────┴─────┐                         │
 │   ┆ └─┬────────┘         │   <b>chell</b>   │     │   <b>ARGUS</b>   │                         │   <i>surfaces: two views of one session</i>
 │   ┆   ┆ ┌──────────┐     │ terminal  │     │  browser  │                         │
 │   ┆   ┆ │ a program│     └─────┬─────┘     └─────┬─────┘                         │
 │   ┆   ┆ └─┬────────┘        ws │                 │ https, then ws                <i>│</i>
 │   ┆   ┆   ┆                    └────────┬────────┘                               │
 │   ┆   ┆   ┆                             └───┐                                    │
 └───┼───┼───┼─────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┘
     ┆   ┆   ┆                                 │  menu: the wire, across a network
 ╔═══╪═══╪═══╪═════════════════════════════════╪══ <b>the bastion</b> ═════════════════════╗   <i>one Linux host: VM, container or metal</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆                                 │                                    ║
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆                     ┌───────────┴───────────┐                        ║
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆                     │         <b>porter</b>        │                        ║   <i>the login page (gdm)</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆                     ├───────────────────────┤    ┌───────────────┐   <i>║   the console's own terminal, on a pty</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆                     │        <b>calypso</b>        ├──┬─┤  <b>chell (pty)</b>  │   <i>║   your session, long-lived (tmux + sshd)</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆               ┌─────┴───────────────────────┤  │ └───────────────┘   <i>║</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆               │                             │  │                     <i>║</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   └┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┤            <b>brasa</b>            │  │ ┌───────────────┐   <i>║   the shell engine (bash + coreutils)</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆                   │                             │  └─┤    <i>the host   │   ║</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆             ┌─────┴─────────────────────────────┤    │ a shell       <i>│   ║   reached by `!`, under host control</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆             │                                   │    │ ~/project     <i>│   ║   the dev environment: edit, build, run</i>
 ║   ┆   └┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┤                <b>fond</b>               │    └───────────────┘   <i>║   the filesystem interface (the VFS)</i>
 ║   ┆                 │                                   │                        ║
 ║   ┆           ┌─────┴───────────────────────────────────┤                        ║
 ║   ┆           │                                         │                        ║
 ║   └┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┤               <b>chris driver</b>              │                        ║   <i>a filesystem driver: CUBE as a tree</i>
 ║               │   salsa   the tree, and its logic       │                        ║
 ║               │   cumin   CUBE's REST, via chrisapi     │                        ║
 ║               └─────────────────────────────┬───────────┘                        ║
 ║                                             │                                    ║
 ╚═════════════════════════════════════════════╪════════════════════════════════════╝
                                               │  HTTPS, Collection+JSON, across a network
                                    ┌─────────────────────┐
                                   ╱                     ╱│
                                  ╱         <b>CUBE</b>        ╱ │
                                 ╱                     ╱  │
                                ┌─────────────────────┐   │
                                │                     │   │                            ChRIS: users, data, plugins, compute,
                                │                     │   ┘                            and the record of every run
                                │       what is       │  ╱
                                │         true        │ ╱
                                │                     │╱
                                └─────────────────────┘
 
 <b>────</b><i>  a call, over a network</i>
 <b>┄┄┄┄</b><i>  the same package, linked into a program of your own: its own engine, its own process</i>
</pre>
    }
    .takeaway{CUBE IS THE ONLY SOURCE OF TRUTH. EVERYTHING ABOVE IT IS A VIEW OF IT.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise, README}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-kernel}
  .title{The Intent Kernel}
  .body{
    .h1{The Intent Kernel}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> brasa --contract}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>intent</b>    ──<u>▶</u>  brasa  ──<u>▶</u>  validated actions  ──<u>▶</u>  CUBE
 <b>receipt</b>   <u>◀</u>──  brasa  <u>◀</u>──  what actually happened
</pre>}
      .o{Say .bf{what} you want, not how.}
      .o{A .bf{bounded} vocabulary. No arbitrary API calls.}
      .o{The engine writes the .bf{receipt}, not the caller.}
      .o{No loops, no .bf{if}. Those stay in your script.}
    }
    .takeaway{NO SURFACE TOUCHES THE RAW API.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise · docs/intent-kernel.adoc}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-intent}
  .title{One Intent, Four Ways}
  .body{
    .h1{One Intent, Four Ways}
    .h2{List one directory under your uploads}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> ls ~/uploads/SAG-anon --from=everywhere}
    .nexus{.id{intent-ways}
      .div{.jump{.target{intent-shell} From the Shell}}
      .div{.jump{.target{intent-program} From a Program}}
      .div{.jump{.target{intent-wire} Over the Wire}}
      .div{.jump{.target{intent-raw} Without mise}}
    }
    }
    .source{harbor-medical-ai.github.io/mise}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{intent-shell}
  .title{From the Shell}
  .body{
    .h1{From the Shell}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chell}
      .o{.typewriter{chris@cube:...loads$ ls -l ~/uploads/SAG-anon
@DIR1  d chris   0        2026-10-16 13:35:18  00005-Synthesized_T1-abcdef0/
@FIL1  - chris   320      2026-10-16 13:35:46  sphere.nii.gz
numbered: @DIR1, @FIL1}}
      .o{One .bf{line}.}
      .o{Handles like .bf{@FIL1} feed the next command.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE COMMAND IS THE INTENT.}
    .source{chell 5.20.7, captured live · harbor-medical-ai.github.io/mise/guide-chell.html}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{intent-program}
  .title{From a Program}
  .body{
    .h1{From a Program}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> cat list.ts}
      .o{
.code{.syntax{language=typescript}
import { chellApi_create, type ChellApi, type TypedEnvelope } from '@fnndsc/brasa';
import type { ListingItem } from '@fnndsc/menu';
/**
 * List the entry names of one ChRIS directory.
 * @param path - Directory to list, as chell would address it.
 * @returns The entry names; empty if the listing failed.
 */
async function directoryNames_list(path: string): Promise<string[]> {
  const sh: ChellApi = await chellApi_create();
  const listing: TypedEnvelope<'fs.listing'> = await sh.ls(path);
  const items: ListingItem[] = listing.model?.data[0]?.items ?? [];
  if (listing.status !== 'ok') return [];
  return items.map((item: ListingItem): string => item.name);
}
}
}
    }
    .takeaway{THE SAME COMMAND, AS A FUNCTION CALL. SHIPPED, IN-PROCESS, ON NODE.}
    .source{typechecked against mise main, not run; assumes a connection made with chrisConnection_init · mise/guide-chell.html}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{intent-wire}
  .title{Over the Wire}
  .body{
    .h1{Over the Wire}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> wscat --connect calypso}
      .o{
.code{.syntax{language=json}
{"type": "execute", "id": "1", "line": "ls /home/chris/uploads/SAG-anon"}
}
}
      .o{
.code{.syntax{language=json}
{"type": "result", "id": "1", "envelopes": [{"status": "ok",
  "model": {"kind": "fs.listing", "data": [{"path": "/home/chris/uploads/SAG-anon",
    "items": [{"name": "sphere.nii.gz", "type": "file", "size": 320}]}]}}]}
}
}
      .o{A .bf{WebSocket} into your live session.}
      .o{Any language can .bf{attach}.}
      .o{Stateless HTTP: .bf{planned}, not shipped.}
    }
    .takeaway{ONE SESSION. ANY SURFACE CAN ATTACH.}
    .source{@fnndsc/menu schemas; exchange derived from them, not captured · mise/guide-session.html}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{intent-raw}
  .title{Without mise}
  .body{
    .h1{Without mise}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> curl cube/api/v1/ --and-then}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>POST</b>  auth-token/                       <i>get a token</i>
 <b>GET</b>   /api/v1/                          <i>discover the file browser</i>
 <b>GET</b>   filebrowser/search/?path=...      <i>find the folder</i>
 <b>GET</b>   folder: children                  <i>subfolders, paged</i>
 <b>GET</b>   folder: files                     <i>files, paged</i>
 <b>GET</b>   folder: link_files                <i>links, paged</i>
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{Six} calls for a small folder.}
      .o{Three lists to .bf{merge} and sort yourself.}
    }
    .takeaway{ONE INTENT, OR A CHAIN OF CALLS.}
    .source{CUBE REST as cumin and salsa call it; folder collections named by link relation}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-session}
  .title{One Session, Many Surfaces}
  .body{
    .h1{One Session, Many Surfaces}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> calypso --berths}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 chell ──┐
         ├──<u>▶</u> <b>calypso</b> ──<u>▶</u> CUBE
 argus ──┘     <i>one login, one session</i>
</pre>}
      .o{Work .bf{outlives} its viewer.}
      .o{Type .bf{cd} in the terminal. The browser moves.}
      .o{Like tmux: close it, .bf{reattach} later.}
      .o{The engine .bf{can} sit where the data stays.}
    }
    .takeaway{TWO VIEWS OF ONE SESSION. NEVER TWO COPIES.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise · docs/calypso.adoc}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-door}
  .title{The Door and the Berth}
  .body{
    .h1{The Door and the Berth}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> porter}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 browser ──<u>▶</u> <b>porter</b> ──<u>▶</u> <b>berth</b> ──<u>▶</u> CUBE
             <i>login page</i>   <i>your session, your container</i>
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{porter}: what gdm is to a desktop.}
      .o{No tokens. No URLs to .bf{copy}.}
      .o{.bf{berth}: your own container. Shipping in stages.}
      .o{Your shell is never on .bf{CUBE's} machine.}
    }
    .takeaway{LOG IN ONCE. LAND IN YOUR OWN SESSION.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise · docs/berths.adoc}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{clinic}
  .title{ChRIS in the Clinic}
  .body{
    .h1{ChRIS in the Clinic}
    .h2{Leg-length discrepancy at Boston Children's}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris feed --from=pacs --run=lld}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 PACS ──<u>▶</u> [pull] ──<u>▶</u> [LLD model] ──<u>▶</u> [measure] ──<u>▶</u> [DICOM report] ──<u>▶</u> PACS ──<u>▶</u> reading room
          └───────────────────<i> one ChRIS feed </i>──────────────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{A study lands. A .bf{workflow} runs. DICOM goes back.}
      .o{The same .bf{container} as on the bench.}
      .o{.bf{Shadow} trial first. Then a clinical trial.}
      .o{The next model .bf{reuses} the plumbing.}
    }
    .takeaway{SAME CONTRACT, FROM THE BENCH TO THE READING ROOM.}
    .source{Tsai, Samal, Lamonica, Morris, McNeil, Pienaar, Eur Radiol 36:1698-1708 (online Sep 2025), doi:10.1007/s00330-025-12022-0}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{clinic-end}
  .title{Where It Has Run}
  .body{
    .h1{Where It Has Run}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --deployments}
      .o{A .bf{laptop}: miniChRIS in docker-compose.}
      .o{On-prem, wired to clinical .bf{PACS}.}
      .o{Mass Open Cloud: OpenShift, .bf{GPUs}.}
      .o{Two hospitals compare. Neither sees the other's .bf{data}.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE CONTAINER DOESN'T CHANGE. ONLY WHERE IT RUNS.}
    .source{FNNDSC/miniChRIS-docker · FNNDSC/CHRIS_docs · Grant, Red Hat Summit 2019 (ChRIS and multi-party compute)}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{harbor}
  .title{Where ChRIS Sits in HARBOR}
  .body{
    .h1{Where ChRIS Sits in HARBOR}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> harbor td --describe}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 ┌─────────────────────────── Hub TD ───────────────────────────┐
 │      marketplace  ·  orchestration  ·  audit  ·  ChRIS       │
 └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
       <u>▼</u> <i>apps and instructions</i>            <u>▲</u> <i>derived results only</i>
 ┌────────────────────────── Spoke TD ──────────────────────────┐
 │  <b>ChRIS</b>:  [app] ──<u>▶</u> [app] ──<u>▶</u> [app]      raw data stays here  │
 │  OpenShift: namespaces, policy, storage                      │
 └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{Apps .bf{move} to the data.}
      .o{ChRIS in .bf{every} TD, Hub and Spoke.}
      .o{The Hub .bf{dispatches}. The Spoke runs.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE SAME WORKFLOW, UNDER THE SAME CHECKS, IN EVERY TD.}
    .source{HARBOR Task Description Document: System Platform}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{harbor-2}
  .title{The Boundary}
  .body{
    .h1{The Boundary}
    .h2{What ChRIS owns in a Trusted Domain, and what it leaves alone}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --scope}
      .o{.bf{Owns}: apps, pipelines, provenance, run history.}
      .o{.bf{Enforces}: what an app may touch.}
      .o{.bf{Leaves}: clusters, fleet, identity, compliance.}
    }
    .takeaway{ChRIS ISN'T COMPETING WITH OPENSHIFT. IT IS THE LAST MILE ON TOP OF IT.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{harbor-end}
  .title{Ingestion as Apps}
  .body{
    .h1{Ingestion as Apps}
    .h2{Every stage of intake is a ChRIS app}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> harbor ingest --stages}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 raw ──<u>▶</u> [validate] ──<u>▶</u> [de-identify] ──<u>▶</u> [deduplicate] ──<u>▶</u> [normalise] ──<u>▶</u> <b>promoted</b>
             │ <i>fail</i>
             <u>▼</u>
       [reject + report]
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{Validate}: readable DICOM, required fields.}
      .o{.bf{De-identify}: headers, burned-in text, pixels.}
      .o{.bf{Deduplicate}: by image content.}
      .o{.bf{Composed} first. Each app then matures.}
    }
    .takeaway{EACH PARTNER'S STAGE IS A CONTAINER WITH A DIRECTORY ON EITHER SIDE.}
    .source{HARBOR Task Description Document: Data Management}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{roadmap}
  .title{What HARBOR Adds to ChRIS}
  .body{
    .h1{What HARBOR Adds to ChRIS}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --gaps --scale=federation}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>Hub</b>         dispatch · telemetry · one record per run
    │ <i>run</i>                      <u>▲</u> <i>status, progress, failure</i>
    <u>▼</u>                          │
 <b>Spoke</b>       [app] ──<u>▶</u> [app] ──<u>▶</u> [app] ──<u>▶</u> provenance ──<u>▶</u> OpenLineage
    │
 <b>OpenShift</b>   pods · storage · isolation
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{Dispatch}: submit at the Hub, run in a Spoke.}
      .o{.bf{Telemetry}: one record per run.}
      .o{.bf{Recovery}: a Spoke stalls, the run resumes.}
      .o{.bf{Baseline} first. Then measure at scale.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE CONTRACT IS PROVEN. RUNNING IT ACROSS A FEDERATION IS THE FUNDED WORK.}
    .source{HARBOR Task Description Document: App Runtime}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{roadmap-peer}
  .title{One ChRIS to Another}
  .body{
    .h1{One ChRIS to Another}
    .h2{Today, only as a client}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --talk-to=another-chris}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
    <b>Hub</b>                                                <b>Spoke TD</b>
 ┌────────────┐        REST, as a <b>CUBE</b> user        ┌────────────────┐
 │  a client  │ ─────────────────────────────────<u>▶</u> │      <b>CUBE</b>      │
 │   chell,   │                                    ├────────────────┤
 │  a script  │ <u>◀</u>═══════ ws: one session ════════<u>▶</u> │    <b>calypso</b>     │
 └────────────┘  <i>command lines in, envelopes out</i>   └────────────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{REST}: any program, as a CUBE user.}
      .o{.bf{WebSocket}: attach to a session at the Spoke.}
      .o{Either way a .bf{client}. Never a peer.}
    }
    .takeaway{TODAY ONE ChRIS CAN ONLY BE A CLIENT OF ANOTHER.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise · docs/calypso.adoc, packages/menu/src/messages.ts}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{roadmap-peer-2}
  .title{The Gaps Between Them}
  .body{
    .h1{The Gaps Between Them}
    .h2{The wire was built for a person at a prompt}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> diff operator hub}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
              <i>today</i>                      <i>a Hub needs</i>
 <b>identity</b>     a user's login             to act as itself
 <b>request</b>      a command-line string      a typed, versioned call
 <b>delivery</b>     one live session           submit once, resume, retry
 <b>egress</b>       not yet classified         policy at the Spoke's edge
</pre>}
      .o{A Hub is not a .bf{person}.}
      .o{It cannot borrow someone's .bf{session}.}
    }
    .takeaway{SHAPED FOR AN OPERATOR. NOT YET FOR A HUB.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise · docs/calypso.adoc, docs/intent-kernel.adoc}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{roadmap-peer-3}
  .title{From Client to Peer}
  .body{
    .h1{From Client to Peer}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --peer --plan}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>dispatch</b>     Hub ──<u>▶</u> Spoke     a stateless intent call: submit, poll, resume
 <b>telemetry</b>    Spoke ──<u>▶</u> Hub     the session wire: status, progress, failure
 <b>agents</b>       any ──<u>▶</u> either    the same intents, offered as tools
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{Funded}: dispatch, recovery, version agreement.}
      .o{.bf{Planned} in mise: a stateless intent API.}
      .o{.bf{Proposed}: the same intents as MCP tools.}
    }
    .takeaway{TODAY A CLIENT. HARBOR FUNDS THE PEER.}
    .source{HARBOR Task Description Document: App Runtime · mise docs/intent-kernel.adoc}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{roadmap-end}
  .title{Governance and Standards}
  .body{
    .h1{Governance and Standards}
    .h2{Making the record legible outside ChRIS}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --extensions --for=harbor}
      .o{.bf{App policy}: what an app may touch, enforced.}
      .o{.bf{Audit}: every operation logged and versioned.}
      .o{.bf{Lineage}: an OpenLineage-compatible export.}
      .o{.bf{DICOMweb}: QIDO-RS, WADO-RS, STOW-RS.}
    }
    .takeaway{PROVENANCE AN AUDITOR CAN READ WITHOUT LEARNING ChRIS.}
    .source{HARBOR Task Description Document: App Runtime · Services}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{working}
  .title{Working With It}
  .body{
    .h1{Working With It}
    .h2{Bringing a tool into a HARBOR workflow}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris plugin --howto}
      .o{Put the tool in a .bf{container}.}
      .o{Flags and two .bf{directories}. No prompts, no GUI.}
      .o{Describe it in a JSON .bf{descriptor}.}
      .o{.bf{Register} it. Now anyone can use it.}
    }
    .takeaway{TRY THE WHOLE STACK ON A LAPTOP FIRST: miniChRIS.}
    .source{ChRIS Plugin Specification · github.com/FNNDSC/miniChRIS-docker · chrisproject.org}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{working-end}
  .title{What We Need to Agree}
  .body{
    .h1{What We Need to Agree}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> harbor --interfaces --open}
      .o{.bf{Stage contracts}: what sits between two stages.}
      .o{.bf{App policy}: what a stage may touch.}
      .o{.bf{Run record}: status, progress, failure.}
      .o{.bf{Lineage mapping}: a run as OpenLineage.}
    }
    .takeaway{AGREE THE DIRECTORIES AND THE EVENTS. THE REST CAN CHANGE UNDERNEATH.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{conclusions}
  .title{Conclusions}
  .body{
    .h1{Conclusions}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> exit
> questions?}
      .o{A .bf{workflow runtime}. Provenance is the tree it leaves.}
      .o{Clinical AI at Boston Children's, .bf{today}.}
      .o{In HARBOR: repeatable and auditable in every .bf{TD}.}
      .o{Next: one ChRIS as a .bf{peer} of another.}
    }
  }
}
